    "alert_id": "EX3_002",
    "title": "Dyslipidemia and hyperglycemia risk on DTG with obesity",
    "message": "Guidelines note DTG is associated with hyperglycemia in previously non-diabetic adults. Patient has multiple hyperglycemia risk factors: BMI 33, fasting glucose 5.6 mmol/L (borderline), and dyslipidemia (LDL 4.2, total cholesterol 6.4, triglycerides 2.3 mmol/L). Guidelines state clients with 2 or more hyperglycemia risk factors need RBS/FBS monitoring every 3 months for 6 months after DTG initiation. No glucose monitoring has occurred since starting TLD in January 2023. The dyslipidemia itself also warrants assessment and management.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Monitor fasting glucose regularly given obesity and DTG. Evaluate dyslipidemia with repeat lipid panel and consider dietary intervention or lipid-lowering therapy per standard guidelines.",
